{
  "abstract": "For finite classical random variables A, B and C, subentropy satisfies Q(AB) + Q(BC) ≥ Q(B) + Q(ABC). Equality holds exactly when A is a function of B almost surely or C is a function of B almost surely. For every t ≥ 0, the pointwise inequality also holds for unnormalized nonnegative tables.",
